+# Exponentially tilted measures
runs/20261007-companion-priority/pbps-b4-corrector-perturbation72/independent-source72/final-inputs/15.exactraw.snapshot:12: trailing whitespace.
+
runs/20261007-companion-priority/pbps-b4-corrector-perturbation72/independent-source72/final-inputs/15.exactraw.snapshot:13: trailing whitespace.
+The exponential tilting of a measure `μ` on `α` by a function `f : α → ℝ` is the measure with
runs/20261007-companion-priority/pbps-b4-corrector-perturbation72/independent-source72/final-inputs/15.exactraw.snapshot:14: trailing whitespace.
+density `x ↦ exp (f x) / ∫ y, exp (f y) ∂μ` with respect to `μ`. This is sometimes also called
runs/20261007-companion-priority/pbps-b4-corrector-perturbation72/independent-source72/final-inputs/15.exactraw.snapshot:15: trailing whitespace.
+the Esscher transform.
runs/20261007-companion-priority/pbps-b4-corrector-perturbation72/independent-source72/final-inputs/15.exactraw.snapshot:16: trailing whitespace.
+
runs/20261007-companion-priority/pbps-b4-corrector-perturbation72/independent-source72/final-inputs/15.exactraw.snapshot:17: trailing whitespace.
+The definition is mostly used for `f` linear, in which case the exponentially tilted measure belongs
runs/20261007-companion-priority/pbps-b4-corrector-perturbation72/independent-source72/final-inputs/15.exactraw.snapshot:18: trailing whitespace.
+to the natural exponential family of the base measure. Exponentially tilted measures for general `f`
runs/20261007-companion-priority/pbps-b4-corrector-perturbation72/independent-source72/final-inputs/15.exactraw.snapshot:19: trailing whitespace.
+can be used for example to establish variational expressions for the Kullback-Leibler divergence.
runs/20261007-companion-priority/pbps-b4-corrector-perturbation72/independent-source72/final-inputs/15.exactraw.snapshot:20: trailing whitespace.
+
